# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Spanish with Emma — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development, or add the same
# variables in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# EVERYTHING IS OPTIONAL. With no variables at all, the whole game works:
# lessons, speaking practice (the device's own speech recognition), Emma's
# voice (the device's own voices), reviews, games and the guided
# conversations. The keys below only switch on extra, server-powered features.
#
# Keys are read ONLY on the server (API routes in app/api). They are never sent
# to the browser — the browser only learns *whether* a feature is available.
#
# Capabilities are read when the app is built, so after changing a variable on
# Vercel, redeploy.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Free conversation with Emma (Talk to Emma → "Chat freely") ───────────────
# An Anthropic API key (https://console.anthropic.com/). Without it, the free
# chat topics are hidden and the guided conversations are used instead.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. The Claude model Emma uses. Default: claude-opus-5
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5


# ── Emma's natural voice (optional, recommended) ────────────────────────────
# Without these, Emma speaks with the device's built-in voices (on iPhone:
# Mónica for Spanish, and Fiona for Scottish English if you download her in
# Settings → Accessibility → Spoken Content → Voices → English).
#
# ElevenLabs is the primary provider: a young, warm, natural Scottish voice for
# Emma's English and a Castilian voice for her Spanish. Audio is streamed, so
# she starts talking while the rest of the sentence is still being generated.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# Emma's voice. Set ONE voice ID to use for both languages…
EMMA_VOICE_ID=
# …or set separate voices (these win over EMMA_VOICE_ID):
# EMMA_ENGLISH_VOICE_ID=   (Scottish English)
# EMMA_SPANISH_VOICE_ID=   (Castilian Spanish — recommended for the best Spanish)
#
# How to get a voice ID (see "Choosing Emma's voice" in the README):
#   • ElevenLabs → Voices → Voice Library → search "Scottish", filter Female /
#     Young, preview, "Add to my voices", then ⋯ → Copy voice ID; or
#   • Voices → Voice Design, describe her ("A warm, friendly young woman in her
#     twenties from Edinburgh with a soft, natural Scottish accent…"), save it,
#     then copy its voice ID.
# With a key but no voice ID, the app uses ElevenLabs' premade voice "Lily"
# (pFZP5JQG7iQjIQuC4Bku) — warm and British, but NOT Scottish. It's only a
# stand-in so the key works straight away; Settings shows a reminder.

# Optional. Default: eleven_multilingual_v2 (most natural). For the lowest
# latency use eleven_flash_v2_5 (or eleven_turbo_v2_5).
# ELEVENLABS_MODEL=eleven_multilingual_v2

# Fallback provider — OpenAI text-to-speech, steered to a Scottish English and a
# Castilian Spanish accent with instructions. One key also enables cloud speech
# recognition below.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_TTS_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini-tts
# OPENAI_TTS_VOICE=coral

# Which cloud voice to try first: elevenlabs | openai | none
# (default: ElevenLabs if its key is set, then OpenAI). The other configured
# provider is used automatically if the first one fails, and the device voice
# takes over if both do. (TTS_PROVIDER is still accepted as an older name.)
# EMMA_TTS_PROVIDER=elevenlabs

# Older names, still accepted: ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID_EN, ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID_ES


# ── Cloud speech recognition (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Uses OPENAI_API_KEY (gpt-4o-mini-transcribe). Handy for browsers without
# built-in speech recognition (e.g. Firefox) and as a fallback when the device
# recogniser fails. Set to "none" to always use the device.
# OPENAI_STT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini-transcribe
# STT_PROVIDER=


# ── Private deployment (recommended if you add paid keys) ────────────────────
# If set, the AI chat and cloud speech routes require this code. Enter it once
# in the app under Settings → You → Access code. Lessons work without it.
APP_ACCESS_CODE=
